1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:05,000
Το Plex ζήτησε 120€ για να συνεχίσετε να βλέπετε από τις συσκευές σας.
Το πλήρωσα εγώ το ποσό.

2
00:00:05,500 --> 00:00:10,000
Αν χρησιμοποιείτε συχνά και μπορείτε,
 οποιαδήποτε συμβολή θα εκτιμηθεί.

3
00:00:06,360 --> 00:00:09,180
These stupid things are coming right at us,
begging to be killed.

4
00:00:09,180 --> 00:00:12,370
Well, I love it! Let's wipe 'em all out!

5
00:00:14,640 --> 00:00:17,040
I'm not sure which ones
are the real beasts.

6
00:00:19,320 --> 00:00:22,000
Old Man Song's a beast himself!

7
00:00:27,850 --> 00:00:32,340
That takes care of this group.
You really have gotten stronger, Sung!

8
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:35,130
And where did you get such a nice dagger?

9
00:00:36,500 --> 00:00:40,930
Now that I think about it,
you haven't been hurt at all today, Jinwoo.

10
00:00:40,930 --> 00:00:42,730
I-Is that right?

11
00:00:42,730 --> 00:00:45,520
Here's hoping no one ends up needing my help.

12
00:00:45,520 --> 00:00:47,990
Well, I'm still counting on you.

13
00:00:47,990 --> 00:00:50,700
<i>He definitely has changed.</i>

14
00:00:51,310 --> 00:00:56,120
<i>Not just his appearance but even his aura...
He's making it look easy now.</i>

15
00:00:56,120 --> 00:00:58,580
Did you start learning martial arts?

16
00:00:59,210 --> 00:01:01,120
Let's keep going.

17
00:02:33,920 --> 00:02:35,220
The path splits here.

18
00:02:35,830 --> 00:02:38,050
The dungeon's been easier than forecast,

19
00:02:38,050 --> 00:02:40,210
so it should be fine
to split into three groups.

20
00:02:40,210 --> 00:02:44,530
There'd be additional risk,
but we'd be able to finish sooner, too.

21
00:02:44,530 --> 00:02:45,940
I think that's a good idea.

22
00:02:46,290 --> 00:02:48,860
I'll take the prisoners down
the path on the right.

23
00:02:48,860 --> 00:02:52,360
If you find the boss chamber,
send someone to let us know.

24
00:02:52,820 --> 00:02:56,740
<i>I guess it's because I raised my perception
ability, but I can tell already.</i>

25
00:02:57,640 --> 00:02:59,410
<i>The boss is down there.</i>

26
00:03:00,210 --> 00:03:02,770
<i>These goblins weren't getting me
much experience, anyway.</i>

27
00:03:03,400 --> 00:03:04,550
Mr. Song.

28
00:03:04,550 --> 00:03:06,610
Let's head down the path to the left.

29
00:03:06,610 --> 00:03:07,500
Understood.

30
00:03:07,500 --> 00:03:09,550
That leaves the middle for us.

31
00:03:09,550 --> 00:03:10,590
Right.

32
00:03:21,690 --> 00:03:24,230
If these goblins are all
there is, we'll be fine.

33
00:03:24,230 --> 00:03:27,340
I just hope we can finish this job safely.

34
00:03:27,340 --> 00:03:28,570
I'm sure we will.

35
00:03:29,320 --> 00:03:33,150
The Weakest Hunter only gets called in
for low-rank dungeons, right?

36
00:03:33,150 --> 00:03:37,260
Except we made that same assumption
once already, and look what happened.

37
00:03:39,850 --> 00:03:40,820
I've made up my mind.

38
00:03:41,380 --> 00:03:45,670
When this raid's over,
I'm gonna apologize to Sung.

39
00:03:46,920 --> 00:03:50,920
It's been bugging you, too, right?
How we ran away.

40
00:03:51,720 --> 00:03:54,160
We're grown men, professional hunters...

41
00:03:54,930 --> 00:03:57,120
Even if it was because of our families,

42
00:03:57,120 --> 00:04:00,400
that doesn't change the fact that
we left one of our own behind.

43
00:04:00,760 --> 00:04:05,100
If we wanna keep being hunters...
we need to face up to what happened.

44
00:04:07,310 --> 00:04:09,690
You think he'll forgive us?

45
00:04:09,690 --> 00:04:13,600
There's no chance.
But I'm still gonna apologize.

46
00:04:14,100 --> 00:04:16,020
Come on, let's get going.

47
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:21,670
What a joke! These goblins are way too easy!

48
00:04:22,000 --> 00:04:23,530
Is that all of them?

49
00:04:23,530 --> 00:04:25,250
You expected it to take longer?

50
00:04:25,250 --> 00:04:27,240
I wanna rack up some more kills!

51
00:04:29,500 --> 00:04:31,830
What if you were facing humans?

52
00:04:32,910 --> 00:04:34,590
Could you kill them just as easily?

53
00:04:35,690 --> 00:04:38,050
I don't really see the difference.

54
00:04:38,050 --> 00:04:40,330
Yeah. It's all the same shit.

55
00:04:41,510 --> 00:04:43,270
What did you want to discuss?

56
00:04:44,410 --> 00:04:47,730
Three men... assaulted my daughter.

57
00:04:48,200 --> 00:04:50,470
She hung herself afterwards,

58
00:04:50,470 --> 00:04:52,980
and my wife was hospitalized
from the psychological shock...

59
00:04:52,980 --> 00:04:58,490
But these scum will be free in a few years,
like nothing happened at all!

60
00:04:58,490 --> 00:05:01,490
Not only that, but they're hunters!

61
00:05:01,950 --> 00:05:04,530
Hunters are allowed to participate
in raids while incarcerated

62
00:05:04,530 --> 00:05:06,600
to reduce their sentences, right?

63
00:05:07,470 --> 00:05:09,530
In what world is that fair?

64
00:05:09,530 --> 00:05:12,510
When my daughter will never get to come home!

65
00:05:15,330 --> 00:05:16,340
And that is?

66
00:05:16,340 --> 00:05:18,630
I have three billion here.

67
00:05:18,980 --> 00:05:21,830
I want you... to...

68
00:05:22,620 --> 00:05:24,460
kill them, please.

69
00:05:25,420 --> 00:05:29,680
What happens in a dungeon
stays in the dungeon, right?

70
00:05:30,270 --> 00:05:33,180
Please! I'm begging you!

71
00:05:36,270 --> 00:05:39,900
Here's what I'll tell the inspectors
when I get out of here:

72
00:05:40,250 --> 00:05:45,480
The three of you were set upon
by a pack of a hundred goblins.

73
00:05:46,740 --> 00:05:49,200
This path really goes all over the place...

74
00:05:49,200 --> 00:05:51,190
Are we even making any progress?

75
00:05:51,190 --> 00:05:53,420
You think we got the dud route?

76
00:05:53,420 --> 00:05:54,830
Here we go...

77
00:05:57,410 --> 00:05:59,250
Help... me...

78
00:05:59,250 --> 00:06:01,510
Hoping for a quick death?

79
00:06:01,960 --> 00:06:06,750
I was actually asked to make you
suffer as much as possible first.

80
00:06:06,750 --> 00:06:08,740
Wh-What the hell are you doing?

81
00:06:10,040 --> 00:06:12,640
Huh. I guess the paths met back up.

82
00:06:12,960 --> 00:06:16,960
Which means the left path
was the one that led to the boss room.

83
00:06:17,490 --> 00:06:19,500
That'll save me some trouble.

84
00:06:19,500 --> 00:06:20,630
Hel—

85
00:06:21,850 --> 00:06:23,860
Guess I'll have to alter my plans.

86
00:06:29,540 --> 00:06:33,800
<i>That Kang Taeshik guy visited me in
the hospital with his inspector boss.</i>

87
00:06:34,750 --> 00:06:37,580
<i>I hope he doesn't remember me.</i>

88
00:06:39,530 --> 00:06:40,420
Mr. Song!

89
00:06:40,420 --> 00:06:41,320
Right!

90
00:06:47,030 --> 00:06:48,760
What is this?

91
00:06:51,120 --> 00:06:52,260
Jeongho!

92
00:06:55,000 --> 00:06:56,400
Mr. Kang...?

93
00:07:09,620 --> 00:07:12,120
Mr. Kim?

94
00:07:12,910 --> 00:07:14,870
Joohee, heal him.

95
00:07:15,470 --> 00:07:16,940
Hurry and heal him!

96
00:07:16,940 --> 00:07:18,540
R-Right!

97
00:07:21,570 --> 00:07:23,960
Mr. Kim! Please hang on!

98
00:07:24,280 --> 00:07:27,180
<i>This wasn't the work of a magic beast.</i>

99
00:07:27,620 --> 00:07:32,140
<i>The weapon's too sharp. And whoever used it
avoided finishing him off... multiple times.</i>

100
00:07:32,590 --> 00:07:37,100
Don't... bother. I'm not gonna make it.

101
00:07:37,750 --> 00:07:39,470
What are you talking about?

102
00:07:39,900 --> 00:07:43,180
You need to survive.
You have a family, don't you?

103
00:07:44,020 --> 00:07:45,570
You...

104
00:07:45,570 --> 00:07:51,030
You need to survive, no matter what!
How else can I keep blaming you?

105
00:07:51,850 --> 00:07:55,500
I'm sorry. I really am sorry.

106
00:07:55,500 --> 00:07:59,830
I didn't see it playing out like this.

107
00:08:00,460 --> 00:08:04,170
I wanted to give you... a proper apology.

108
00:08:04,870 --> 00:08:08,140
I'm real sorry, kid.

109
00:08:08,760 --> 00:08:11,240
I mean... it...

110
00:08:19,650 --> 00:08:21,000
Kim...

111
00:08:30,380 --> 00:08:32,530
Wow, you're fast.

112
00:08:34,530 --> 00:08:37,910
I had intended on taking out
the healer first...

113
00:08:39,250 --> 00:08:41,670
But it looks like you were able
to change her fate.

114
00:08:42,160 --> 00:08:45,030
Mr. Kang? Did you do this?

115
00:08:45,030 --> 00:08:46,380
What if I did?

116
00:08:46,380 --> 00:08:49,690
Aren't you from the Hunter's Association?

117
00:08:49,690 --> 00:08:51,080
You think you can get away with—

118
00:08:51,080 --> 00:08:53,050
I've got the perfect little story.

119
00:08:53,860 --> 00:08:59,560
I was gonna say that it was a swarm
of goblins, but here's my new angle:

120
00:09:00,220 --> 00:09:04,710
The prisoners were plotting an escape,
so they killed the rest of you

121
00:09:04,710 --> 00:09:09,150
and then tried to ambush me while
I was occupied fighting the boss...

122
00:09:09,530 --> 00:09:14,740
But they didn't have what it takes.
And that's why I was the sole survivor.

123
00:09:14,740 --> 00:09:16,580
What do you think? Perfect, huh?

124
00:09:17,040 --> 00:09:18,200
You scum.

125
00:09:18,910 --> 00:09:22,370
You can't stand against him. I'll go.

126
00:09:23,500 --> 00:09:25,300
I'm borrowing this, Kim.

127
00:09:26,230 --> 00:09:28,800
<i>I haven't raised a sword against
another person in a long time.</i>

128
00:09:29,170 --> 00:09:32,250
<i>He's B-Rank, a level above me. But still...</i>

129
00:09:32,810 --> 00:09:36,250
Ms. Joohee, could you cast a
physical strength buff on me?

130
00:09:36,250 --> 00:09:37,600
R-Right!

131
00:09:37,880 --> 00:09:40,970
<i>Assassin types tend to have weak defenses.</i>

132
00:09:41,440 --> 00:09:43,100
<i>I'll aim for that.</i>

133
00:09:43,100 --> 00:09:48,360
A washed-up mage like you trying to rely
on strength instead is gonna backfire.

134
00:09:48,360 --> 00:09:50,740
Right now, I'm a swordsman.

135
00:09:53,360 --> 00:09:57,740
But your skills are magic-focused!
Taking up that sword won't help you!

136
00:10:00,890 --> 00:10:02,960
You might be surprised!

137
00:10:03,520 --> 00:10:05,080
Okay, you've got some moves.

138
00:10:05,540 --> 00:10:09,090
Even putting aside the buff,
you really do know your stuff.

139
00:10:09,620 --> 00:10:12,340
<i>It was only for a moment,
but he was able to keep up.</i>

140
00:10:13,420 --> 00:10:15,180
<i>If Mr. Song was a little faster...</i>

141
00:10:15,180 --> 00:10:19,600
Fast and accurate! I can see why
you ditched magic for the sword!

142
00:10:20,830 --> 00:10:23,040
But that's about all you can manage.

143
00:10:27,400 --> 00:10:29,150
That pain-in-the-ass healer.

144
00:10:29,470 --> 00:10:31,360
Guess I had better deal with her after all.

145
00:10:35,820 --> 00:10:38,490
Turning your back on an armed opponent?

146
00:10:38,490 --> 00:10:41,580
I guess you're no average old fart.

147
00:10:41,940 --> 00:10:44,820
I've trained S-Rank hunters before!

148
00:10:44,820 --> 00:10:47,080
In terms of blade technique, I won't be beat!

149
00:10:47,370 --> 00:10:50,870
Maybe, but the powers you've
been given have their limits.

150
00:10:51,250 --> 00:10:56,760
Did you think a mage type like you
could keep up with an assassin hunter?

151
00:11:01,460 --> 00:11:02,570
Mr. Song!

152
00:11:04,860 --> 00:11:05,890
Oh, no...

153
00:11:05,890 --> 00:11:09,360
Your healer's useless, too.

154
00:11:13,280 --> 00:11:14,560
Game over.

155
00:11:21,700 --> 00:11:22,830
<i>Did that work?</i>

156
00:11:23,240 --> 00:11:27,120
You took up that sword to make me
lower my guard against magic...

157
00:11:27,620 --> 00:11:30,920
so that when I went for the kill,
you could blast me.

158
00:11:30,920 --> 00:11:35,220
Pretty slick plan, for a senile old bastard.

159
00:11:35,220 --> 00:11:36,800
<i>I'm finished!</i>

160
00:11:37,740 --> 00:11:38,390
Now die.

161
00:11:44,850 --> 00:11:46,710
You again?

162
00:11:46,710 --> 00:11:47,940
Who the hell are you?

163
00:11:48,950 --> 00:11:52,100
Sung Jinwoo, E-Rank.

164
00:11:53,420 --> 00:11:56,950
E-Rank? That's a load of crap.

165
00:11:56,950 --> 00:12:00,160
Sung? What was that just now?

166
00:12:00,160 --> 00:12:05,160
I could see a power type, even at E-Rank,
being able to block like that.

167
00:12:05,160 --> 00:12:09,070
But the reaction time you'd
need to pull it off twice...

168
00:12:09,070 --> 00:12:10,170
would require an assassin build.

169
00:12:10,590 --> 00:12:15,260
Not that it really matters, anyway.
You've been hiding your skills, haven't you?

170
00:12:15,260 --> 00:12:17,680
Your little group seems to know each other.

171
00:12:17,680 --> 00:12:22,480
So you can't be a false ranker.
They don't let any witnesses live.

172
00:12:22,480 --> 00:12:25,290
Which leaves only one possibility...

173
00:12:26,010 --> 00:12:27,440
You had a second awakening.

174
00:12:27,440 --> 00:12:28,520
You did, Sung?

175
00:12:28,520 --> 00:12:29,690
A second awakening?

176
00:12:30,390 --> 00:12:33,820
Then it must've happened
after the double dungeon!

177
00:12:34,160 --> 00:12:35,730
<i>A double dungeon?</i>

178
00:12:36,040 --> 00:12:39,090
<i>Wait... Is he that weakling
E-Rank from before?</i>

179
00:12:39,680 --> 00:12:42,890
<i>But he looks and acts like a different person.</i>

180
00:12:42,890 --> 00:12:45,700
<i>And the mana meter only read 10
when we checked back then.</i>

181
00:12:46,180 --> 00:12:48,260
<i>If he had a second awakening,
it must have been after.</i>

182
00:12:48,260 --> 00:12:51,670
<i>So how'd he survive the double dungeon...?</i>

183
00:12:52,130 --> 00:12:56,740
Well, whatever happened to you, I can tell
you don't have a ton of hunting experience.

184
00:12:56,740 --> 00:12:59,590
So it falls to me to teach you the ropes.

185
00:12:59,980 --> 00:13:01,680
Why did you do this?

186
00:13:01,680 --> 00:13:03,760
You mean killing the prisoners?

187
00:13:04,250 --> 00:13:07,560
I was asked to by the father of their victim.

188
00:13:07,560 --> 00:13:11,210
They drove someone to suicide
and didn't regret it at all.

189
00:13:11,210 --> 00:13:13,150
It's a bit of social justice, that's all.

190
00:13:13,150 --> 00:13:15,900
No. I was talking about Mr. Kim and Mr. Kang.

191
00:13:16,270 --> 00:13:17,440
Why kill them?

192
00:13:18,110 --> 00:13:21,660
Was it to silence them? Because you
could've done that without torturing them.

193
00:13:22,220 --> 00:13:26,360
But you didn't do that. You toyed with them.

194
00:13:26,910 --> 00:13:29,620
I don't think you did this
for the victim's sake at all.

195
00:13:30,120 --> 00:13:32,080
That's not what you really want.

196
00:13:34,650 --> 00:13:38,030
Sure, I can do that.

197
00:13:38,450 --> 00:13:40,490
But you've got the wrong idea.

198
00:13:41,010 --> 00:13:45,470
I'm a B-Rank hunter who has received
offers from a number of major guilds.

199
00:13:46,150 --> 00:13:50,420
So why am I working for peanuts
in the Hunter's Association?

200
00:13:50,930 --> 00:13:57,690
It's because I find people a <i>whole</i>
lot more fun to kill than beasts!

201
00:14:00,840 --> 00:14:03,750
There's a limit to what even a
reawakened E-Rank can pull off!

202
00:14:05,800 --> 00:14:06,620
Too slow.

203
00:14:06,620 --> 00:14:07,990
Impressive.

204
00:14:11,520 --> 00:14:13,160
He's so agile!

205
00:14:13,630 --> 00:14:17,570
Nothing at all like the Sung I remember!

206
00:14:20,260 --> 00:14:21,970
<i>We're matched in speed!</i>

207
00:14:22,400 --> 00:14:25,840
<i>We've got the same build
and similar skill levels...</i>

208
00:14:26,170 --> 00:14:29,490
<i>But I have far more experience battling
high-ranked opponents than you!</i>

209
00:14:29,490 --> 00:14:32,480
<i>That inexperience will be your downfall!</i>

210
00:14:38,900 --> 00:14:41,910
You've got grit, I'll give you that.

211
00:14:41,910 --> 00:14:43,310
Sorry...

212
00:14:43,310 --> 00:14:43,860
Eh?

213
00:14:43,860 --> 00:14:46,870
But could you be a little less bloodthirsty?

214
00:14:47,570 --> 00:14:51,040
Now you've done it.
Even the system's noticed.

215
00:14:52,370 --> 00:14:54,970
Then again, I guess I should be grateful.

216
00:14:54,970 --> 00:14:58,590
The system's given me another reason
to make sure you die.

217
00:14:58,590 --> 00:15:00,250
The system?

218
00:15:00,250 --> 00:15:01,670
<i>What the hell is he talking about?</i>

219
00:15:02,080 --> 00:15:04,630
<i>I should have the advantage here...</i>

220
00:15:11,150 --> 00:15:12,680
<i>He's even faster?</i>

221
00:15:13,600 --> 00:15:16,650
<i>Poison? A special effect
from that dagger of yours?</i>

222
00:15:21,230 --> 00:15:23,990
<i>I've got something special to show you, too!</i>

223
00:15:25,530 --> 00:15:27,030
<i>He vanished?</i>

224
00:15:27,420 --> 00:15:30,990
I should be completely undetectable.
You're a sharp bastard, all right.

225
00:15:31,400 --> 00:15:36,440
This is the Stealth skill. It conceals
my sight, my sound, and even my smell.

226
00:15:36,440 --> 00:15:40,740
Only a tiny fraction of assassin
hunters ever obtain this skill.

227
00:15:40,740 --> 00:15:45,480
Of course, no one knows I can use it, either.

228
00:15:45,480 --> 00:15:46,520
And the reason for that...

229
00:15:48,770 --> 00:15:53,720
is that no one who's seen me use it
has ever lived to tell the tale.

230
00:15:54,300 --> 00:15:56,230
You won't be so fast now.

231
00:15:56,850 --> 00:15:57,850
Jinwoo—

232
00:15:57,050 --> 00:15:58,760
Keep your hands to yourself!

233
00:15:59,610 --> 00:16:02,150
You two are next.

234
00:16:02,570 --> 00:16:05,070
<i>At this rate, Sung's going to die!</i>

235
00:16:05,070 --> 00:16:09,290
Now, think you can dodge my next strike
with an injured leg?

236
00:16:09,290 --> 00:16:12,240
Are you done talking now?

237
00:16:12,600 --> 00:16:14,030
Full recovery.

238
00:16:16,160 --> 00:16:18,000
<i>He healed in an instant?</i>

239
00:16:18,000 --> 00:16:22,340
<i>I've never heard of a combat hunter
who could use healing magic, too.</i>

240
00:16:22,650 --> 00:16:24,460
<i>What else does he have?</i>

241
00:16:24,460 --> 00:16:27,550
<i>He's impossible to predict!
This guy is dangerous!</i>

242
00:16:27,890 --> 00:16:30,120
<i>That's another of my emotions, gone.</i>

243
00:16:30,970 --> 00:16:34,850
I don't even need to get angry
to kill filth like you.

244
00:16:36,240 --> 00:16:40,020
Oh, I see. You've killed before, too, huh?

245
00:16:41,670 --> 00:16:44,120
Man, I didn't know we were
in the same business!

246
00:16:44,520 --> 00:16:45,770
<i>I see now.</i>

247
00:16:45,770 --> 00:16:50,610
<i>He must've been forced through a number
of grave decisions in a short time.</i>

248
00:16:51,020 --> 00:16:53,830
<i>It wasn't just his appearance that changed.</i>

249
00:16:53,830 --> 00:16:58,580
When hunters awakened, their supernatural
abilities turned the world on its head.

250
00:16:59,120 --> 00:17:03,590
Where we are is a place that only hunters
can enter. Laws aren't worth shit here.

251
00:17:03,820 --> 00:17:06,160
Whoever's strongest comes out on top.

252
00:17:11,740 --> 00:17:15,710
<i>Is he tracking me from my bloodlust?</i>

253
00:17:15,710 --> 00:17:18,990
<i>But that won't let him know
exactly where I'm coming from!</i>

254
00:17:23,980 --> 00:17:25,200
What the—

255
00:17:27,150 --> 00:17:29,780
Wait... Are you kidding me?

256
00:17:33,140 --> 00:17:36,560
What... the hell...

257
00:17:42,570 --> 00:17:45,720
You asked why I killed them, right?

258
00:17:46,500 --> 00:17:52,660
It's pointless to expect hunters, who thrive
in mortal combat, to stick to normal morals.

259
00:17:53,300 --> 00:17:59,470
You're the same way. You and me,
we're killing machines at this point.

260
00:17:59,910 --> 00:18:02,910
Which is why I'll die. Because I lost.

261
00:18:02,910 --> 00:18:05,560
It's just natural selection.

262
00:18:06,260 --> 00:18:08,460
But what the hell are you?

263
00:18:08,460 --> 00:18:12,030
You've got assassin skills,
healing, and debuffs...

264
00:18:12,030 --> 00:18:13,530
I've never heard of anything like it.

265
00:18:13,910 --> 00:18:17,940
Couldn't tell you. I'd like to know, myself.

266
00:18:22,290 --> 00:18:28,210
Well, you just killed me,
so your little E-Rank act is over.

267
00:18:28,210 --> 00:18:32,280
Let's say that I'm a hunter
who gets stronger with every battle.

268
00:18:35,140 --> 00:18:39,960
Then I'd say your shadow stretches
into some really nasty places...

269
00:18:40,440 --> 00:18:44,340
and you'll probably get as strong
as those places are dark.

270
00:18:44,730 --> 00:18:47,400
You'd better watch yourself, though.

271
00:18:48,200 --> 00:18:55,880
If you gaze for long into an abyss,
the abyss... gazes also into you.

272
00:19:01,870 --> 00:19:05,970
<i>He's right. I'm incomparably strong
next to how I was before.</i>

273
00:19:06,640 --> 00:19:08,210
<i>But for some reason...</i>

274
00:19:08,880 --> 00:19:14,330
<i>the stronger I get, the more I feel
something inside of me falling apart.</i>

275
00:19:14,330 --> 00:19:15,550
Jinwoo!

276
00:19:15,550 --> 00:19:17,420
Thank you so much.

277
00:19:17,830 --> 00:19:22,230
You really did it.
We only survived because of you.

278
00:19:22,230 --> 00:19:25,590
It's fine. You two should exit the dungeon.

279
00:19:26,300 --> 00:19:27,730
I'll handle the rest.

280
00:19:27,730 --> 00:19:30,020
What? By yourself?

281
00:19:30,710 --> 00:19:32,610
Then again... you're right.

282
00:19:33,470 --> 00:19:37,240
It's a shame we won't be able
to lay Kim and Kang to rest.

283
00:19:37,240 --> 00:19:38,700
We'll be waiting outside.

284
00:19:50,540 --> 00:19:51,630
Manager Woo!

285
00:19:51,630 --> 00:19:53,970
I heard the report. Where are the survivors?

286
00:19:53,970 --> 00:19:55,340
Right this way.

287
00:19:55,340 --> 00:20:01,050
<i>I can't believe Kang was
killing in secret all this time.</i>

288
00:20:01,400 --> 00:20:06,760
<i>He had always been a little sketchy,
but as his supervisor, I was too careless.</i>

289
00:20:07,610 --> 00:20:09,100
This is the three of them.

290
00:20:10,930 --> 00:20:14,280
<i>Isn't he... the E-Rank hunter from before?</i>

291
00:20:14,750 --> 00:20:16,360
<i>He looks like a whole different person.</i>

292
00:20:17,240 --> 00:20:18,760
It's good to see you again.

293
00:20:18,760 --> 00:20:20,660
Aren't you the inspector...?

294
00:20:20,660 --> 00:20:25,400
Woo Jinchul. I want to apologize for what
one of my men put you through.

295
00:20:26,050 --> 00:20:29,920
But first... I'd like
to address the main issue.

296
00:20:29,920 --> 00:20:33,380
Which one of you defeated Kang?

297
00:20:33,380 --> 00:20:36,460
<i>I guess I won't be able to keep
my secret any longer.</i>

298
00:20:36,970 --> 00:20:41,390
<i>Which means I'm gonna have to
cancel my deal with Jinho...</i>

299
00:20:42,010 --> 00:20:43,350
It was me.

300
00:20:43,810 --> 00:20:46,320
I killed Mr. Kang.

301
00:20:46,680 --> 00:20:49,020
Pardon me, but I believe your rank was...?

302
00:20:49,020 --> 00:20:50,540
C-Rank.

303
00:20:50,540 --> 00:20:53,560
How were you able to beat
a B-Rank like Kang?

304
00:20:53,560 --> 00:20:56,280
Why, with the help of my friend here.

305
00:20:57,450 --> 00:21:01,490
I see. Then you say you
managed with a healer's help.

306
00:21:02,580 --> 00:21:05,170
<i>Kang was the cream of the crop among B-Ranks.</i>

307
00:21:05,170 --> 00:21:08,710
<i>By all rights, a C-Rank mage
shouldn't have stood a chance...</i>

308
00:21:10,130 --> 00:21:11,540
Very well.

309
00:21:11,540 --> 00:21:16,000
I'll need to write this incident up,
so if you could please come with me.

310
00:21:16,400 --> 00:21:19,860
<i>I can't get cocky just because
I beat Kang Taeshik.</i>

311
00:21:20,180 --> 00:21:24,060
<i>I couldn't tell before,
but this guy is A-Rank.</i>

312
00:21:24,060 --> 00:21:26,200
<i>As it stands, I'd be helpless against him.</i>

313
00:21:27,580 --> 00:21:30,360
Sorry if I overstepped my bounds there.

314
00:21:31,270 --> 00:21:35,230
But I imagine you've got a good reason
for keeping your strength hidden.

315
00:21:36,880 --> 00:21:40,700
Well, think of it as my way
of paying you back.

316
00:21:45,090 --> 00:21:46,530
<i>Three hours later,</i>

317
00:21:46,530 --> 00:21:50,250
<i>the man who hired Kang Taeshik
to kill the prisoners turned himself in,</i>

318
00:21:50,250 --> 00:21:52,830
<i>which confirmed that
we acted in self-defense.</i>

319
00:21:54,920 --> 00:21:56,880
What a day, huh?

320
00:21:57,630 --> 00:21:58,800
Jinwoo.

321
00:22:00,360 --> 00:22:03,950
Do you remember this?
